# Build outputs. An APK committed once is in the history forever and bloats every
# clone; the Release page is where artifacts belong.
*.apk
*.aab
*.so

# Signing material. These patterns exist BEFORE any keystore does -- committing a
# release key even once means it is in the git history permanently, and the signing
# certificate is one of exactly three things about an Android app that can never be
# changed after the first install.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
keystore.properties

